Z||000000||ckphoto@nac.net||10-24-2001||11:51 AM||||Hi guys glad I found this place<BR>I have 84 fiero based ferrari which I am trying to correct problems on<P>OK the head lights are in the up position<BR>I found coming off the back of the motor is a <BR>blue/white wire connected to a fusible link<BR>there is also a connector with on gray and one green  not connected to anything I have tracked down the pink red black plug<BR>now from looking at the diagram in the hays manual it appears as the actuator relays have been removed for some reason I want to confirm before ordering that these plugs will mate with the relay or is something else missing<BR>thanks for any help<BR>chris||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||10-24-2001||06:03 PM||||Ordinarily, on the 1984-86 headlight system, there is an actuator relay mounted on each headlight assembly, and <B>two</B> connectors plug into the bottom of each relay.  In addition, each motor has a blue wire - but without the fusible link you describe.<P>Try the following link for help; it has lots of useful information: <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/headlight.htm</A>   With that, and the wiring diagrams you say you have, you should be able to get things working.  Or at least, figure out what you need.  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ckphoto@nac.net||10-24-2001||06:15 PM||||Thanks<BR>great page you posted will help greatly<BR>chris||||reg||14
